,"subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aaronp64/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I tried adding these to the C++ tests, but it looks like calling `set` or `get` with an invalid index in C++ will just crash.  Binding for gdscript gets around this with some macros defined in variant_call.cpp, so it'll give an error message instead.\r\n\r\nI added `array_bad_index` gdscript tests for this case for `get`/`set`/`operator[]`.  Not sure if this is expected, but the `operator[]` error handling is different from the others - `get()` and `set()` will print an error and continue running, while `operator[]` has a different error format and stops running.","created_at":"2025-08-30T17:14:05Z","updated_at":"2025-08-30T17:14:05Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110097#discussion_r2312027616","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110097","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2312027616"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110097#discussion_r2312027616"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110097"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2312027616/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":203,"original_start_line":198,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":210,"original_line":210,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2311281402,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":63,"position":68,"subject_type":"line"}]